INT. STADIUM CONCOURSE - IMPROVISED TRIAGE - NIGHT

A concrete ring under flickering sodium lights. Hot-dog stands turned into supply desks. Cots in rows where the beer lines used to be. The air smells of antiseptic and popcorn.

DR. SAOIRSE KELLEHER, 40s, scrubs smeared with someone else's blood, kneels at a cot. Red hair under a surgical cap. Her eyes never stop moving.

BARTOSZ NOWAK, 50s, a stocky nurse with a grey ponytail, wrestles an IV pole across the cracked floor.

LIN WEI, 20s, paramedic in a drenched jacket, runs a gurney in, rain streaming off her shoulders.

On the gurney: ODALYS MERCEDES, 60s, grey-faced, one hand clamped on her chest. Her lips are blue.

FINN ASHFORD, 20s, a first-year resident with a nervous goatee, trails behind, clutching a chart he can't read.

LIN WEI
Sixty-two female, chest pain, pulse thready, pressure seventy over forty!

SAOIRSE
Put her here. Bart, line.

BARTOSZ
Working on it.

FINN
(overlapping)
Should I call cardiology? Is cardiology even here?

SAOIRSE
Finn, no. Get the crash cart.

ODALYS
(weak)
I'm fine. I'm fine, I just need to sit.

SAOIRSE
Mrs. Mercedes, you are sitting. Stay with me.

LIN WEI
She's been like this since the underpass!

BARTOSZ
Line's in. Pushing fluids.

FINN
Crash cart's in the lobby, I'll--

SAOIRSE
Run.

He runs. Odalys's eyes roll back. The monitor squeals into a flatline.

LIN WEI
Doctor!

SAOIRSE
Compressions. Bart, count!

BARTOSZ
One, two, three--

Saoirse locks her hands over the old woman's chest and pushes. Ribs crack. Nobody blinks.

FINN
(returning, out of breath)
Cart!

SAOIRSE
Charge to two hundred.

LIN WEI
Clear!

The body jumps. The monitor stays flat.

SAOIRSE
Again.

A long beat. A blip. Another. A rhythm stumbles back to life.

BARTOSZ
Sinus. We have sinus.

Saoirse sits back on her heels. Lin Wei laughs, a wet, startled sound. Finn lowers the paddles, shaking.

ODALYS
(whispering)
Told you. Fine.
